    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Over the last 20 years, China has put a lot of effort into protecting wetlands. All that hard work has "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The world’s first international "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "mangrove",
            "zh": "红树林"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " centre was "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in Shenzhen. Why do mangroves matter? And why did Shenzhen stand out?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Mangroves play an important role worldwide. They take "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "carbon dioxide",
            "zh": "二氧化碳"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from the air and then store it for thousands of years. Studies show that they can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " five times as much carbon as rainforests. People often call mangroves “coast guards.” As global warming raises sea levels, these trees could help "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " coastal cities from flooding. What’s more, mangroves offer shelter to animals. Many birds, for example, stop there during their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "migrations",
            "ref": "v-migration"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Mangroves "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " an area of about 14.8 million "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "hectares",
            "zh": "公顷"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " worldwide. However, they’re "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from many places. China is one of the few countries where mangrove areas are "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Their total area has risen from 22,000 hectares in 2001 to 29,200 hectares today. Shenzhen is home to 296.18 hectares of mangroves and has put in a lot of work to protect them in recent years. This has helped bring back 43.33 hectares of mangroves. Take Futian Mangrove Ecological Park, for example, where nearly 100,000 birds "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the winter. Among them, there are more than 20 "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "rare",
            "ref": "v-rare"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "endangered",
            "ref": "v-endangered"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " species."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Building the Shenzhen centre is important,” said a Chinese official. “It serves as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for China to work with other countries in protecting mangroves.” Shenzhen isn’t going to stop there, however. It plans to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " itself into an international wetland city by 2035. By then, half of its wetlands will be protected."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
